{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":491294,"name":"Shaun Bowe","username":"Shaun_Bowe","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/shaun_bowe/{size}/120884_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-14T22:32:47.795Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWindows GrokBot Desktop app\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nI have a routine that is triggered by a webhook. Previously when I clicked Edit on a routine it would show me the webhook url and security token. Now when I click edit It just types in the Bot’s window Edit your routine: {routine name}. I have no way to get the webhook information.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate a routine by prompting the bot to create a routine that is triggered by a webhook.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWait for the routine to be created on the right hand panel.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick the Routine name to open the edit pane.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou will see the text that describes what the routine does\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick the Edit button at the bottom of that pane\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe pane does not flip to edit mode\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nPreviously the UI would display the schedule and any important information about the routine including the webhook url and Bearer Token\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nIf applicable, attach images or videos (.jpg, .png, .gif, .mp4, .mov)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOperating System\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan c